<details class="model-disclosure reasoning-help" id="reasoning-help">
	<summary>Reading statements and reasoning</summary>
	<div class="disclosure-body">
		<p>Reading order introduces ideas; it does not make one statement follow from the previous one. Recorded arguments identify which premises are used together for a conclusion.</p>
		<p><strong>Deductive</strong> means the argument claims its conclusion must follow if its premises are true. <strong>Defeasible</strong> means the reasoning can be overturned by new evidence, alternatives, or context.</p>
		<p>Statement type identifies a claim, definition, value, or strategy. Confidence reports its current justification separately. Inclusion in this Model identifies a working commitment; neither inclusion nor an inference label confirms an empirical claim.</p>
	</div>
</details>
